messages:
cara_sales: Piotr reported a streaming failure during the pilot demo. Android webview client shows JSON parse errors and the stream drops after about 40s. Demo stalled.
ben_se: Any request IDs or client logs? Is this reproducible?
piotr_customer: Reproducible on our embedded webview only. Desktop browsers fine. Client error: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseChunk (main.min.js:412)". Network shows SSE events with data lines split mid-object.
leo_oncall: Infra side: I see a spike of 503s and a few upstream "connection reset by peer" from the edge proxy around the same timeframe. Also a short surge of 429s for the customer's org key. Could be proxy buffering triggering truncation plus retry overload.
ben_se: Two-pronged: (1) client assumes each data event is complete JSON and calls JSON.parse immediately, (2) network/proxy can fragment events or close streams early under load.
piotr_customer: Sample (from network tab):

event: message
data: {"id":42,"text":"Start of a long message...\n\n"}

event: message
data: {"id":43,"text":"continued but we see it trun\n\n"}

The second data payload is truncated and the client tries to parse it.
ben_se: Short-term fix for you: have the SSE handler buffer consecutive `data:` payloads and attempt JSON.parse only when buffer yields valid JSON. Also disable aggressive client-side retries for streaming endpoints.
leo_oncall: On our side I'm applying a throttling rule for that org to reduce retry storms and disabling proxy buffering for streaming routes on canary. I'll also add a heartbeat comment (":\n") every 15s to keep connections alive.
ops-bot: canary v2.16.0 deployed to eu-west-2 at 2105200000
cara_sales: Piotr — want us to apply the infra tweak and send the small snippet for your wrapper?
piotr_customer: Yes please. Wrapper patching is tedious but we can inject a tiny JS shim in the webview.
ben_se: Snippet to share (tiny accumulator):
```
let buf = '';
function onSseData(line) {
  buf += line;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    onMessage(obj);
    buf = '';
  } catch(e) {
    // wait for more data
    if (buf.length > 64*1024) { buf = ''; }
  }
}
```
Add a 5s flush timeout to avoid stuck buffers.
leo_oncall: Actions: (1) infra throttle and disable proxy buffering for streaming (applied to canary) (2) send heartbeat comments every 15s (in progress) (3) add metric for partial-parse rate (queued).
cara_sales: Thanks all. I'll coordinate patch rollout with Piotr and follow up tomorrow before the exec demo. Marking POC as high priority. :thumbsup:
piotr_customer: Applying proxy tweak now, will test and report in ~25m. Thanks team.
